  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Consider a function $f:{R}^{2\\times 3}\\to {R}^{2}$ defined by\n\n$$\nf(A)=A[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven that ${a}_{ij}$ denotes the entry of $A$ in the intersection of the $i$th row and $j$th column, we have\n\n$\\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{a}_{12}}=${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "We can write the function $f$ as\n\n$$\nf(A)=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} & {a}_{13} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} & {a}_{23}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{11}+2{a}_{12}+{a}_{13} \\\\ 3{a}_{21}+2{a}_{22}+{a}_{23}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{a}_{12}}=\\frac{∂}{∂{a}_{13}}(3{a}_{21}+2{a}_{22}+{a}_{23})=0.\n$$",
